      "name": "NICE NG228 — Subarachnoid haemorrhage caused by a ruptured aneurysm: diagnosis and management",
      "year": 2022,
      "section": "Suspect SAH with thunderclap headache (sudden, severe, peaking within minutes); non-contrast CT head immediately; if CT is normal and done more than 6 h after onset, consider lumbar puncture at least 12 h after onset; if SAH confirmed: CT angiography and discussion with a neurosurgical centre; nimodipine",
